Missing: the menu of distinct referents for an identifier in a macro body

ADR-0027 (accepted 2026-09-20) says an identifier inside a macro body resolves to
every meaning its expanding CUs give it, and that the browser menu shows them all,
deduped by referent. Nothing implements that yet; this test is the specification.

`next` in node.h is a field of struct list_node in list.c and of struct tree_node
in tree.c. Both are true. What happens today, cold:

    <bottom-information len=<n>>No reference</bottom-information>
     <symbol line=2 type=macro selected=1 base=0 drefn=0 refn=0 len=<n>>NEXT</symbol>

So the push finds nothing, and the one menu row is the MACRO, not either field.
Two separate causes:

1. findMacroExpansionFile (src/cxref.c) reads a UsageMacroBaseFileUsage marker,
   which expandMacroCall records only when options.mode == XrefMode (src/yylex.c),
   so a cold server has none. Hence "No reference".
2. That marker holds ONE file per macro by construction - addMacroBaseUsageRef
   skips an existing one (src/yylex.c:2481) and writeCxReferenceBase writes at
   most one per symbol (src/cxfile.c:366) - so even completing it cannot answer
   which CUs expand a macro.

The menu row for NEXT comes from findMacroExpansionFile's side effect: it filters
through createSelectionMenu (src/cxref.c:2200), which also adds each matching item
to the session menu. That is what makes a macro body answer with the browser
instead of going through the ordinary cardinality rule.

The fix, three steps, one test each:

1. findMacroExpansionFile stops adding to the session menu, so a macro body falls
   through to olcxShowSelectionMenu() like every other push: one referent is a
   goto, several are the menu. Pinned by test_browsing_push_in_unexpanded_macro.
2. The marker lookup becomes a walk over the includers of the file defining the
   macro. collectIncludersOfStaleHeader (src/server.c:277) already walks that
   graph for entry refresh Pass 3. This removes the XrefMode dependency and
   un-suspends test_browsing_push_in_unexpanded_macro_without_create.
3. The walk runs to the bound and collects EVERY expanding CU, deduped by
   referent. That is what this test asks for. Remove this .suspended in that
   commit.

To verify when it goes green, because these are guesses:
- The <symbol> attribute values in `expected` are invented. Take drefn/refn and the
  row indentation from a real run; test_browsing_cexercise:303 is the model, where
  two struct fields named `next` render as `<struct>.<field>` with no leading space,
  while the macro row above has one.
- `-olcxmenufilter=0` is MenuFilterAllWithName. Whether 0 or 1 is right here is
  unchecked.
- Rename must refuse from inside a macro body (ADR-0027). Not covered by this test.
